So len <= size. But in the loop, ep is text + size - 11 * len. So if len is 2 and size is 100, ep is text + 100 - 22 = text + 78. So tp starts at text + 2. If during the loop, tp is advanced to text + 102, which is beyond ep (text +78), but the loop condition is tp <= ep. However, the loop condition is checked only at the start of the iteration. So during the current iteration, after advancing tp beyond ep, the code continues processing, leading to out-of-bounds accesses.

